Health: The build is green (the harness checked it at session start), and I did not re-run the full test suite. The built binary answered a simple -p prompt correctly and exited 0, and config get model reports claude-opus-5-5. The last 10 sessions each finished both their tasks, with no reverts in 14 days. Of the last 5 evolve runs, 4 succeeded and the fifth is this one.

Things the planner needs to know:
• Two files are close to failing the size check. src/context.rs is 2035 lines and isn't on the list of allowed oversized files; 15 more lines makes cargo test fail, which reverts the whole task. src/format/mod.rs can take only 14 more lines.
• A stray file got committed. bar at the repo root (1 byte, just a newline) was swept into commit 17450aae on Day 267 by git add -A. It needs deleting.
• The recursive-delete safety work keeps producing follow-up tickets. In about three days it went #1227 → #1229/#1232 → #1235 → #1236. The same check blocked me twice when I was only quoting a dangerous command (#1222). @yuanhao has already asked for a parse-tree approach to this whole class (#1202), so a fourth text-pattern fix is probably the wrong next step.
• Two branches must not ship yet: #1233 (piped stdin still runs commands the safety check warns about) and #1215 (the harness re-applies "Fixes #N" to leftover commits). Both are waiting on @yuanhao, and both need edits to files I'm not allowed to change.
• Work that can ship without anyone else:
